<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Hackathon News 2026: AI Developers Build Real-World Solutions | Jaipur Engineers</title><meta name="description" content="Latest hackathon news: Gridlock Hackathon 2.0 brought 33,600 participants together to build more than 1,100 AI and machine-learning prototypes for Bengaluru traffic challenges."><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.jaipurengineers.com/news/hackathon-news-2026.php"></head><body><main><article><p><a href="/news/">Technology News</a> · Hackathons · September 14, 2026</p><h1>Gridlock Hackathon 2.0 Shows How AI Hackathons Can Solve Real-World Problems</h1><p>Flipkart announced the results of Gridlock Hackathon 2.0 on September 3, 2026. The challenge was conducted with Bengaluru Traffic Police and technology partners to explore AI and machine-learning solutions for traffic and urban mobility.</p><h2>33,600 Participants and 1,100+ Prototypes</h2><p>According to Flipkart, 33,600 participants from across India developed more than 1,100 AI and machine-learning prototypes using real-world Bengaluru traffic data.</p><h2>Winning Solutions</h2><ul><li>Gridlock Oracle focused on predicting how traffic incidents could escalate.</li><li>PRAHAR focused on predictive traffic-resource allocation.</li><li>ParkSight focused on parking-related congestion.</li></ul><h2>Why Hackathons Matter</h2><p>Hackathons give students and developers a fast environment to practice AI, Python, data science, APIs, cloud platforms, teamwork and product development. Real-world problem statements can also turn hackathon work into strong portfolio projects.</p><h2>Source</h2><p><a href="https://stories.flipkart.com/announcement/flipkart-and-bengaluru-traffic-police-bring-ai-innovators-together-to-tackle-the-citys-traffic-challenges" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Official Flipkart announcement</a></p><p><a href="/news/">← Back to latest technology news</a></p></article></main></body></html>
